{
  "phase": 420,
  "slug": "explicit-range-build-flag",
  "title": "Forward an explicit default-off dense writer selector through Vite and Docker",
  "sourceFiles": [
    "Dockerfile",
    "vite.config.ts",
    "vite/accountRetentionFlags.ts",
    "vite/rangeBuildFlags.test.ts",
    "docs/release-validation-graph.json"
  ],
  "requiredChecks": [
    "checked-types",
    "checked-focused",
    "final-quality",
    "final-format",
    "final-registry",
    "final-inventory",
    "final-inventory-controls"
  ],
  "detail": "A strict0/1 accountRangeFlags policy captures RANGE_RECEIVE with ordinary default0; the actual Vite config installs it and Docker forwards ARG(default0) through build-stage ENV before pnpm build. Writer-off does not disable compatible readers. All original retention/resume/history policies, Vite configuration and Docker bytes remain exact after removing only the explicit new selector/function/two forwarding lines. No runtime source, encoding, authority, owner, budget or deadline changes.",
  "validation": "The initial six-red build test includes two new assertions that incorrectly compare an ES-module namespace with a plain object; those are corrected to compare exported scalar values, retaining the failed attempt. Corrected before has four failures for missing explicit definition/default/validation and Docker forwarding, while both raw local-environment compilations already work: Vite previously exposed an explicit local VITE value automatically. This does not establish prior Docker support. After the change, six new controls pass through the actual config, including production-mode on/off compiled probes with reader1, immutable captured selection, invalid-value refusals and independent Docker mapping. Initial new-test typing of optional config.define is corrected without app changes; the red log remains. Types and21cases/four files pass, with all prior build-policy and writer controls untouched. Independent AST review preserves both old policies and the complete config except selector; Docker comparison retains every old byte. Quality, format,17registry checks, inventory and10controls pass; no runtime/crypto hashes, domains or construction moves. Graph adds one required five-declaration/six-case file.",
  "summary": "The selected writer flag now has a strict explicit Vite path and Docker ARG/ENV forwarding, ordinary default0 and unchanged readers. Six new build controls plus existing policies total21passing cases, with types/bookkeeping checks green. Runtime source is byte-identical to419.",
  "limitations": "Production-mode unit compilation is not an image or lifecycle proof. The same-tree writer-off rollback image, real marked/dense/stale-tab opening, ordinary legacy operation and cold/Undo are still required. Latest full unit checkpoint remains419:329files/3204pass/one skip128.78s; it predates the new six-case build test. Real peer/Worker B fairness/past-index and Stage5/6 remain. No format/trust/runtime/limit/gate/deadline change, commit, publication or deployment.",
  "decisionTitle": "Make dense writer activation explicit in both build entry paths",
  "decision": "Use a strict captured build selector with ordinary default0 and Docker forwarding, preserving reader compatibility independently. Local Vite raw environment exposure was already possible; distinguish that observation from the previously absent Docker path. Keep actual writer-on/off image and lifecycle evidence separate from configuration-unit proof.",
  "next": "Prove first-floor lifecycle with genuine composed peer/Worker dense admission, then31s interior cold, frozen old readers/pending writing, actual stale-turn idle audit and the same-tree writer-off rollback image. Correct any implementation defect within the approved format and existing native/authentication guards; stop only at the operator decision/unfixable boundaries. Continue automatically after each freeze.",
  "progressEdits": [
    [
      "Ordinary builds remain writer-off; Docker/Vite forwarding and the selected\nwriter-on/writer-off build proofs remain.",
      "Ordinary builds remain writer-off. Docker/Vite forwarding is covered in420;\nselected writer-on/writer-off image and lifecycle proofs remain."
    ]
  ],
